      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{23}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe entry in row $3$, column $3$ is $0$. Switching rows $2$ and $3$ therefore makes $a_{23}=0$.\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2}.\n$$",
